														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1963963">
									

<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">That's what they do, except for releasing him. They infect him, then amnesticize him enough to erase the self-propagating pattern, but not enough to effect his long-term memory. Then they keep him around in case they need him, in case other versions show up. Otherwise they'd have to wait until someone properly awful with the appropriate musical background came along and use him. But what do they do in the meantime? Constantly infect and then cure a string of D-Class to keep the new version on lockdown until an orchestra conductor goes postal? It seems much cheaper to me to hold on to this one guy that can already do what they need.</span></p>
<p>EDIT: Personnel status modified pursuant to Ethics Committee recommendations.</p>

